<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila bans pork imports from Germany, Netherlands.</title>
<headline>Manila bans pork imports from Germany, Netherlands.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philippine Agriculture Secretary Salvador Escudero has ordered a ban on the importation of live pigs and pork products from Germany and the Netherlands due to the reported outbreak of swine fever in both countries.</p>
<p>Escudero ordered the Philippine Bureau of Animal Industry to &quot;stop issuing permits for the importation of live pigs and pork products from Germany and the Netherlands&quot;, a statement from the secretary dated March 18 but only released on Wednesday said.</p>
<p>In the statement, Escudero said he issued the order on the recommendation of Philippine Agriculture Attache Dalmacio Salting who reported an outbreak of swine fever in Germany in the middle of January and the detection of the disease in the Netherlands in early February.</p>
</text>
